The items include the number itself, and every number that ends with "1" (ie the ones digit). For example, "Africa" (the continent) ends with a 1. So does "one". So does "one". But "20" does not end with a 1, and the final part of the answer would be "Africa".
   // Then there are:
   //        1                                "one"             "20"
   // Africa                 end with a 1
   // Africa               ends with a 1         1                  "20"

It would be more correct to say that the scan ranges from 1 to 100.
